The far2l terminal-extension support (including the far2l shared
clipboard) is derived from the putty4far2l project. The far2l PuTTY
extensions were originally written by Ivan Sorokin; the putty4far2l
fork was created by unxed <https://github.com/unxed/putty4far2l> and
forward-ported to PuTTY 0.78.5 by Ivan Shatsky
<https://github.com/ivanshatsky/putty4far2l>. The far2l file manager
itself is by elfmz and contributors <https://github.com/elfmz/far2l>.
These contributions are likewise released under the MIT licence below.

The session-scripting engine is the RuTTY patch, copyright 2013-2014
Ernst Dijk. It reached this port as part of KiTTY, which is distributed
under the MIT licence; the RuTTY sources themselves carry a copyright
notice and no licence text, so his notice is reproduced here as it
stands rather than restated in other terms.

The base64 codec of the far2l support (kitty/far2l/cencode.c and
cdecode.c) is from the libb64 project, which placed it in the public
domain.

One part is under its own terms instead of the licence below: the
regular-expression matcher of the URL detection (kitty/url/re_lib) is
Henry Spencer's V8 regexp, copyright (c) 1986 by University of Toronto,
written by Henry Spencer and not derived from licensed software. Its
notice in kitty/url/re_lib/regexp.c grants use and free redistribution
on three conditions. The author is not responsible for the consequences
of use. The origin must not be misrepresented. Altered versions must be
plainly marked. This copy is altered (KiTTY's hyperlink patch and two
memory fixes of this port). Each change is marked in that file.

